Answer a load cancelled before its task ran with 409, not a dropped reply

The scheduler spawns a play's or cache command's background load with
the HTTP reply inside the task, wrapped in PendingReply, whose drop
answers "Load cancelled before playback" (409). The wrapping happened
in the task's body, so it only took effect once the runtime first
polled the task. A stopall, fadeall or shutdown that aborted the task
before that dropped the bare reply sender instead, and the HTTP client
got a 500 "Command was dropped before completion".

PendingReply is now built before the task is spawned and moved into
it, so dropping a never-polled task answers 409 like any other
cancelled load.

Found while writing the scheduler's characterization tests, which
aborted loads straight after submitting them.

Tests (failing before the fix with the reply dropped unanswered): a
stopall sent before a play's load task has run answers the play 409; a
shutdown abort before a precache's task has run answers it 409.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
and a warning-free release build (RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings); fuzz suite 7
